/-
This module proves that on an infinite domain, a universal property provides strictly more information than any finite set of value checks. Specifically, if a property P fails to hold universally but holds on a finite set S, there must exist a counterexample outside S. This formalizes the intuition that property testing covers "infinitely more" cases than unit testing.
-/

import Mathlib

